["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/webpage", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "A Uniform Resource Locator (URL) that can be used to locate a resource, as defined in [RFC 9110](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/rfc9110/) Section 4.2.1 or Section 4.2.2. It may include an optional fragment identifier as specified in [RFC 3986](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/rfc3986) Section 3.5.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ismn", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Standard Music Number (ISMN)](https://ismn-international.org/ismn/the-ismn/) is a unique numeric identifier for printed music (notated music) standardized by [ISO 10957](https://www.iso.org/standard/83122.html). It consists of either 10 characters (starting with the letter \"M\" for assignments prior to January 1, 2008) or 13 digits. A 13-digit ISMN is composed of four parts: the GS1 prefix `979-0`, a registrant element, an item element, and a check digit. While elements may be divided by spaces or hyphens for human readability, these separators shall be omitted when the identifier is stored electronically (e.g., `9790006538424`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType/conformsTo", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The `from` Element conforms to each `to` /FunctionalSafety/Assumption or Specification.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/byteRange", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/PositiveIntegerRange", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/SupplyChain/DestroyProcess", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The destruction process is defined in this process.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
